    [Doc][Model] Update MiniMax-M3 A3 prefill recommendations (#18427)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    Update the MiniMax-M3 A3 prefill recommendation from DP2/TP4/PP2 to
    DP1/TP4/PP4, with a `16,15,15,14` split of the 60 transformer layers.
    Keep the launch command, both sides of the Mooncake configuration, proxy
    endpoints, and KV Cache Pool examples consistent with the 16-NPU node
    layout.
    
    Set the A3 Prefill examples' `--max-num-batched-tokens` to `8192`. Add
    comments recommending `8192` for input lengths >= 8192 tokens and the
    input token length for shorter inputs. Remove the explicit
    `--long-prefill-token-threshold 2048` so it does not cap prefill chunks
    below the recommended token budget.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    Documentation only: updates the recommended A3 prefill configuration and
    tuning guidance.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - `bash format.sh ci` — all checks passed.
    - `git diff --check` — passed.
    - Syntax-checked all six modified Bash examples and parsed all four A3
    P/D KV transfer configurations as JSON.
    - Smoke-tested the documented launcher with a stub `run_dp_template.sh`:
    DP1/TP4/PP4 assigns NPUs 0–15 to one Prefill rank on port 31050.
    Verified the proxy uses one Prefill endpoint and four Decode endpoints.
    - Verified that the Chinese `.po` file matches the original base version
    and the Markdown configuration changes are preserved.
    
    No model inference or NPU performance benchmarks were run for this
    documentation-only change.
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/8cc9aa5ad350f6f80cf3bebb298d410803ff75a9
    
    Signed-off-by: LostFox11 <wangziyue17@huawei.com>
    Co-authored-by: LostFox11 <wangziyue17@huawei.com>

